<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/"
                  xmlns:cat-harness.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/processes/ns/"
                  id="Definitions_Process_KgSeparation" targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="1">
  <bpmn:import namespace="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/" location="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns.jsonld" importType="http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="administrator" name="Administrator"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="authoring-agent" name="Authoring agent"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="build-pipeline" name="Build pipeline"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="platform-authoring-agent" name="Platform authoring agent"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="publication-manager" name="Publication manager"/>
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_Process_KgSeparation">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_Process_KgSeparation" name="A knowledge graph leaves for its own repositories" processRef="Process_KgSeparation"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_KgSeparation" name="A knowledge graph leaves for its own repositories" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Move part of a knowledge graph into repositories of its own: the content (files to read, no code) and its tools (the code that writes and checks it) separate as a pair, into two repositories, not one. `kg-separation.md` is the practice; this is its order and its gates. Stages 1-3 are `graph-detanglement`, reused rather than restated.

EVERY GATEWAY IS A COMMAND. `Tools closed?` is `check:tools-closure` with the content's no-code test and a byte-identity check on the generated files; `Every identifier its file's path?` is `check:node-iris`; `Green alone?` is the standalone rehearsal; `Ready to seed?` is `seed:ready --layer &lt;name&gt; --rehearse`, decided by decisions/seed-readiness-gate.dmn. A check that could not run stops the process rather than reading as clean.

A PERSON DECIDES FOUR TIMES, AND THE ADMINISTRATOR LANE SAYS WHERE: whether to separate at all, whether to authorise the extraction, creating the repositories, and the cutover. Nothing is committed to the new repositories before they are created, and the parent keeps its own copy until it consumes the first release.

VERSIONS: the pair starts at the content's version at the split, then each is versioned on its own; a tools release lists the content majors it supports. Examples: bootstrap and bootstrap-tools; cat-harness and cat-harness-tools.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <cat-harness.processes:policy enforcement="strict"/>
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_Process_KgSeparation">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Agent" name="Authoring agent" partitionElementRef="authoring-agent">
        <bpmn:documentation>Briefs, measures the signals, runs declare-detangle-isolate, reports what would move, seeds the repositories once they exist, and adopts each later release. Verification is always by re-running a gate, never by a change looking right.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_Trigger</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Brief</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Measure</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Detangle</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Propose</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Drain</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Seed</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Platform" name="Platform authoring agent" partitionElementRef="platform-authoring-agent">
        <bpmn:documentation>The platform-side stages: the graph's identity (version, iriBase, nodeSchemas), moving harness output about it into the host, splitting the content from its tools, and making the parent consume the pair additively.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Identity</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Hosted</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Split</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Consume</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Publication" name="Publication manager" partitionElementRef="publication-manager">
        <bpmn:documentation>Owns where things are published: every identifier the content mints must be a file some step publishes, at /&lt;version&gt;/ for programs and /v&lt;major&gt;/ for people; and the first release.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Plan</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Release</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Pipeline" name="Build pipeline" partitionElementRef="build-pipeline">
        <bpmn:documentation>Runs the checks that decide the gateways: the tools' import closure and the content's lack of code, node identifiers against file paths, the standalone rehearsal, and dereferencing after release. A gate that cannot tell stops the process; it never reads as clean.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Closed</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Ids</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Rehearse</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Alone</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Unknown</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_SeedReady</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_SeedUnknown</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Verify</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_CutoverCheck</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_CutoverComplete</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_CutoverUnknown</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Admin" name="Administrator" partitionElementRef="administrator">
        <bpmn:documentation>The person's decisions: whether to separate at all, authorising the extraction, creating the repositories, and the cutover that retires the parent's copy. An agent reports and waits at each; none of them may be relaxed by a package.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Decide</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Stays</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Authorise</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Declined</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Create</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Cutover</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Separated</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>

    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_Trigger" name="Too large, or readers&#10;and cadence differ">
      <bpmn:outgoing>F0</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_Brief" name="Brief the work" calledElement="GT_Brief">
      <bpmn:documentation>Here the work is a separation: what is separating, and why.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F1</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:incoming>F0</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Measure" name="Measure the signals">
      <bpmn:documentation>Files and bytes per instance, clone cost (`bun run cat health`), gate time, merge contention, the candidate's cohesion and cut (`kg:detangle`), wrong-direction edges, and the would-be tools package's import cone. Recorded in the work context; none alone is a trigger.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="kg-separation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_Decide" calledElement="Process_AskThePerson" name="Separate this graph?">
      <bpmn:documentation>The owner decides from the measured signals, and also decides the address base for its identifiers, where verdicts about it live, and what its tools repository owns. Declining is a real outcome: the graph stays where it is.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="kg-separation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F3</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Stays" name="Stays where it is">
      <bpmn:incoming>F3</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Detangle" name="1–3 · Declare, detangle,&#10;isolate">
      <bpmn:documentation>The graph-detanglement practice, all of its gates: declared in place, zero wrong-direction edges on every axis, and standing alone with its own declaration, namespace and artefact. A plain task on purpose, not a call to graph-detanglement.bpmn: that process ends in its own authorise-and-extract steps, which here are stages 9-13 of this one, and calling it would run them twice.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="graph-detanglement"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>F15</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Identity" name="4 · Identity: version,&#10;iriBase, nodeSchemas">
      <bpmn:documentation>The declaration carries name, version, iriBase, needs and nodeSchemas. A base move is `bun run iri:sync -- --from &lt;old base&gt;`, once; then `iri:sync:check` and `check:node-iris` are green.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="kg-separation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Hosted" name="5 · Move harness output&#10;about it to the host">
      <bpmn:documentation>QA verdicts, translation templates, the exported graph and the glossary ledger are harness output ABOUT the graph: they live with the harness (kgQaHomeFor, translationsHomeFor). The content keeps only what its own checks need; the leak test's pending list is empty. The one exception is a separated layer that declares a `qa` directory of its own with `storage`: its verdicts are its own repository's, published to that repository's qa-reports branch (step 10), and read by a host at the commit it pins.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="kg-separation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Split" name="6 · Split content&#10;from tools">
      <bpmn:documentation>Create &lt;name&gt;-tools as a sibling directory and move the code: the Zod source, the generators, the README and diagram writers, the content checks. Cut its import cone to its own files and declared packages. Both start at the content's version.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="kg-separation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>F9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Closed" name="Tools closed,&#10;content code-free?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Decided by commands, not judgement: `check:tools-closure` (no import leaves the tools directory or names an undeclared package), the content's no-code test, and generated files byte-identical before and after the move. Any failure goes back to the split.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F9</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Plan" name="7 · Plan publication">
      <bpmn:documentation>Every identifier the content mints is a file some step publishes: /v&lt;major&gt;/, for what programs read and pages people read alike; the exact release is the pin's. Name collisions between published files are resolved here.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="instance-publication"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>F12</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F11</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Ids" name="Every identifier&#10;its file's path?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Decided by `check:node-iris`: a published node's own identifier ($id or @id) under the release address must be its file's path. A mismatch goes back to the plan: move the file, or change the identifier before it is ever served.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F11</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F12</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F13</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Rehearse" name="8 · Rehearse standalone">
      <bpmn:documentation>Copy the content and the tools alone into a temporary directory, with nothing else on the path, and run the tools' checks there. An empty tree must exit non-zero, so a rehearsal over nothing cannot pass.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="kg-separation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F13</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F14</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Alone" name="Green alone?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Green with nothing else present goes on. Red means an edge the earlier gates did not see, so back to detangling. If the rehearsal could not run, that is not a pass: stop.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F14</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F15</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F16</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F17</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Unknown" name="UNKNOWN — stop.&#10;Not clean">
      <bpmn:incoming>F16</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_Propose" name="Report what moves&#10;— sizes, what breaks" calledElement="GT_ReportWhatMoves">
      <bpmn:incoming>F17</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F18</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_Authorise" calledElement="Process_AskThePerson" name="9 · Authorise&#10;the extraction">
      <bpmn:documentation>A repository cut changes the substrate every other process binds to; that is a person's decision. Declining leaves the graph declared, detangled, isolated and split in place.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="deletion-requires-confirmation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F18</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F19</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F20</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Declined" name="Stays in place,&#10;ready to leave">
      <bpmn:incoming>F19</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:userTask id="Task_Create" name="Create the&#10;repositories">
      <bpmn:documentation>The owner creates the content and tools repositories and their Pages. Nothing is committed to them before this.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="kg-separation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F20</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F21</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_SeedReady" name="Ready to&#10;seed?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Asked AT SEED TIME, because the tree has moved since `8 · Rehearse`. A seed is a snapshot with no history, so every open PR over the layer when it is taken is orphaned into the monorepo. Computed by decisions/seed-readiness-gate.dmn (hit policy FIRST) from `seed:ready --layer &lt;name&gt;`: an open `heavy-mover` PR over the layer or the next one, any open PR on the next layer, more than five over the layer, any that moves a file in it, a red sibling-layout rehearsal, or a direct dependent that discovery cannot find among sibling clones answers `not yet`. A criterion that could not be decided answers `unknown` and stops; it never hides a finding already certain, which is why the `not yet` rows come first. The rehearsal runs only on request (`--rehearse`), so without it the answer is never `settled`.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <cat-harness.processes:decision ref="decisions/seed-readiness-gate.dmn#Decision_SeedReadiness"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F21</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>F28</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F27</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F29</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F30</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_Drain" name="Drain: land, close or&#10;re-target the open PRs" calledElement="GT_Drain">
      <bpmn:incoming>F27</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F28</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_SeedUnknown" name="UNKNOWN — do not&#10;seed. Not clean">
      <bpmn:incoming>F29</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Seed" name="10 · Seed both&#10;repositories">
      <bpmn:documentation>Seed main, then bring the content and the tools in as reviewed pull requests with their history, so neither repository's first commit is unreviewable. The seed includes every publisher the declaration promises (`sub-kg-lifecycle` stage 10): a `qa` directory with `storage` needs `.github/workflows/publish-qa.yml`, the caller of the tools layer's `layer-qa-publish.yml`, and `test/results/` ignored. Without it the declared store is never written, and once the layer stops committing its results no reader finds them.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="kg-separation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F30</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F22</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_Consume" name="11 · Parent consumes,&#10;additively" calledElement="Process_UpstreamAdoption">
      <bpmn:documentation>The parent pins the pair (a commit while staging, a version once released) — a code dependency as a `source.remote` instance in its root `index.config.json` (remote-mount skill), never a submodule — repoints its imports, and keeps its own copy until it is green with the dependency declared.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="upstream-version-adoption"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F22</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F23</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Release" name="12 · First release">
      <bpmn:documentation>Tag each repository, publish /v&lt;major&gt;/. From here the two are versioned independently; a tools release lists the content majors it supports.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="package-release"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F23</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F24</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_Verify" name="Every identifier&#10;dereferences" calledElement="Process_PublishVerification">
      <bpmn:documentation>After the release is live, every published identifier resolves to the file it names.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="publish-verification"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F24</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F25</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:userTask id="Task_Cutover" name="13 · Cutover: retire&#10;the parent's copy">
      <bpmn:documentation>The one commit worth reverting, made only after the parent consumes the release and every identifier dereferences. It retires the parent's copy, frozen, never refreshed and never rendered, rather than deleting it. Where the copy goes is the sub-kg-lifecycle skill's stage 13; this diagram does not name that store, because the published graph must not.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="deletion-requires-confirmation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F25</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>F33</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F26</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_CutoverCheck" name="Measure the cutover:&#10;separation:cutover:check">
      <bpmn:documentation>Run `bun run cat separation:cutover:check --site` in the SEPARATED repository (Tool `separation-cutover-check`). Six conditions, each decided by an existing gate and none assumed: every declared layer mounted at its pin; every path a declaration names resolves (`check:declaration-resolution` — directories, assets, visualisers, needs); no wiring still names the monorepo (`livesAt`, a submodule, a reusable workflow, a path into the old checkout); no import or reference against the layer order; and the site builds from the mounts alone. A finding inside a mounted layer is upstream's and is listed, not counted.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="kg-separation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F26</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F31</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_CutoverComplete" name="Cutover&#10;complete?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Decided by the exit of `separation:cutover:check`: 0 every condition measured and passed, 1 a condition failed, 2 one could not be determined or was not run (without `--site` the answer is never complete). A failure goes back to the cutover with the findings; an undetermined answer stops, because a cutover that could not be shown complete has not been shown complete.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F31</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F32</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F33</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F34</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_CutoverUnknown" name="UNKNOWN — not shown&#10;complete. Not clean">
      <bpmn:incoming>F34</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Separated" name="Separated">
      <bpmn:incoming>F32</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>

    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F0" sourceRef="Start_Trigger" targetRef="Task_Brief"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F1" sourceRef="Task_Brief" targetRef="Task_Measure"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F2" sourceRef="Task_Measure" targetRef="Task_Decide"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F3" sourceRef="Task_Decide" targetRef="End_Stays" name="declined"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F4" sourceRef="Task_Decide" targetRef="Task_Detangle" name="separate"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F5" sourceRef="Task_Detangle" targetRef="Task_Identity"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F6" sourceRef="Task_Identity" targetRef="Task_Hosted"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F7" sourceRef="Task_Hosted" targetRef="Task_Split"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F8" sourceRef="Task_Split" targetRef="GW_Closed"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F9" sourceRef="GW_Closed" targetRef="Task_Split" name="leaks or stale"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F10" sourceRef="GW_Closed" targetRef="Task_Plan" name="closed"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F11" sourceRef="Task_Plan" targetRef="GW_Ids"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F12" sourceRef="GW_Ids" targetRef="Task_Plan" name="mismatch"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F13" sourceRef="GW_Ids" targetRef="Task_Rehearse" name="every one matches"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F14" sourceRef="Task_Rehearse" targetRef="GW_Alone"/>
